In the Word JavaScript API (Office.js), **`autoFitWindow()`** is a method available on the **`Word.Table`** class[1]. It is used to automatically resize the table columns to fit the width of the document window or page margins (equivalent to the "AutoFit to Window" feature in the Word desktop application)[2][1].

### Syntax
```javascript
table.autoFitWindow();
```

### Example Usage
Here is how you can use `autoFitWindow` within a `Word.run` batch to adjust the first table in a document:

```javascript
await Word.run(async (context) => {
    // Get the first table in the document body
    const table = context.document.body.tables.getFirst();

    // Apply the auto-fit window behavior
    table.autoFitWindow();

    // Synchronize the operations with the Word document
    await context.sync();
    console.log("Table has been successfully fitted to the window.");
});
```

### Requirements
* **Requirement Set:** `Word.Table` features generally map across standard versions, but check your specific project configuration if targeting older clients. 
* **Context:** Like other Office.js mutations, you must call `await context.sync()` to apply the changes to the Word document.

