In the Word JavaScript API (Office.js), `getBorder` is a method used on table-related objects (`Word.Table`, `Word.TableCell`, and `Word.TableRow`) to retrieve a specific border configuration[1]. 

To specify **"All"** borders, you pass `"All"` (or `Word.BorderLocation.all` depending on your environment/types) into the `getBorder()` method[2].

### Example Usage

The following example demonstrates how to use `getBorder("All")` on a table to read or modify its border properties (such as color, type, and width) in Word for Mac or any other supported platform:

```javascript
await Word.run(async (context) => {
    // Get the first table in the document
    const firstTable = context.document.body.tables.getFirst();

    // Retrieve the 'All' border configuration for the table
    // (You can use "All" or Word.BorderLocation.all)
    const allBorders = firstTable.getBorder("All");

    // Load properties you want to read
    allBorders.load(["color", "type", "width", "visible"]);
    await context.sync();

    console.log(`Current Border Type: ${allBorders.type}`);
    console.log(`Current Border Color: ${allBorders.color}`);
    console.log(`Current Border Width: ${allBorders.width}`);

    // Optionally, modify the borders
    allBorders.color = "#000000"; // Black
    allBorders.width = 1.5;       // 1.5 points
    allBorders.type = "Single";   // Single line style

    await context.sync();
});
```

### Key Details:
* **API Version:** `WordApi 1.3` or higher[2].
* **Applicable Objects:** `Word.Table`, `Word.TableRow`, and `Word.TableCell`[1].
* **Other Border Locations:** Aside from `"All"`, accepted string literals for border locations include `"Top"`, `"Left"`, `"Bottom"`, `"Right"`, `"InsideHorizontal"`, `"InsideVertical"`, `"Inside"`, and `"Outside"`[2].

