The search for ""tableColumns" Word for Mac office.js "is not supported" OR "table.columns"" returned the following summary:
If you are encountering an error stating that `tableColumns` or `table.columns` is **"not supported"** in your Office.js Word Add-in on Mac, it is typically caused by one of two reasons:

### 1. Requirement Set Limitation (`WordApiDesktop`)
Features involving direct column collections and manipulation (`table.columns` or `range.tableColumns`) belong to the **`WordApiDesktop`** requirement set (specifically introduced in `WordApiDesktop 1.3`)[1]. 
* **The Catch:** `WordApiDesktop` APIs rely on desktop-specific binaries[2]. While supported on Word for Windows and Mac, your specific version of Word for Mac might be running an older build that hasn't fully integrated that version of the requirement set yet, or your manifest is restricting/failing to load it properly.

### 2. Version and Platform Mismatch (Word for the Web)
If you are testing your Mac-built add-in or running code targeting **Word on the Web (Browser)**, column collection APIs will fail because web browsers do not support desktop-only requirement sets[2]. 

---

### How to Fix / Workaround It

#### Step A: Check for Requirement Set Support First
Always wrap desktop-only table column calls in a capability check so your add-in fails gracefully instead of crashing abruptly on unsupported platforms or older Word versions[2]:

```javascript
if (Office.context.requirements.isSetSupported("WordApiDesktop", "1.3")) {
    await Word.run(async (context) => {
        const table = context.document.body.tables.getFirst();
        const columns = table.columns;
        columns.load("items");
        await context.sync();

        // Your column logic here
    });
} else {
    console.warn("Table columns API is not supported on this version of Word/Platform.");
    // Fallback: Loop through rows and cells instead
}
```

#### Step B: Fallback Strategy (Iterate through Rows and Cells)
