The search for ""paragraphFormat" site:learn.microsoft.com/en-us/javascript/api/word" returned the following summary:
The `Word.ParagraphFormat` class is part of the Word JavaScript API for Office Add-ins[1][2]. It represents the paragraph formatting properties (such as alignment, indents, spacing, and pagination controls) for paragraphs, ranges, or styles[1][2].

### Common Properties
* **`alignment`**: Specifies the alignment for the specified paragraphs (e.g., Left, Centered, Right, Justified)[1].
* **`firstLineIndent`**: Specifies the value (in points) for a first-line or hanging indent (positive for first-line, negative for hanging)[1].
* **`leftIndent` / `rightIndent`**: Specifies the left and right indent values (in points)[1].
* **`lineSpacing`**: Specifies the line spacing (in points)[1].
* **`spaceBefore` / `spaceAfter`**: Specifies the spacing amount before or after the paragraphs[1].
* **`keepTogether`**: Controls whether all lines of the paragraph stay on the same page during pagination[1].
* **`keepWithNext`**: Controls whether the paragraph stays on the same page as the following paragraph[1].
* **`widowControl`**: Controls widow and orphan control[1].

### Example Usage

The following example retrieves and logs the paragraph formatting properties of a custom paragraph style[1]:

```typescript
await Word.run(async (context) => {
    const styleName = "SampleParagraphFormat";
    const sampleStyle: Word.Style = context.document.getStyles().getByName(styleName);
    const paragraphFormat: Word.ParagraphFormat = sampleStyle.paragraphFormat;

    // Load desired properties
    paragraphFormat.load({
        alignment: true,
        firstLineIndent: true,
        leftIndent: true,
        lineSpacing: true,
        spaceAfter: true,
        spaceBefore: true
    });

    await context.sync();

    // Output formatting data
    const formatData = paragraphFormat.toJSON();
    console.log("Paragraph format properties:", formatData);
});
```

You can also apply formatting updates directly using the `.set()` method on a paragraph's format object:

```typescript
await Word.run(async (context) => {
    const paragraph = context.document.getSelection().paragraphs.getFirst();

    paragraph.paragraphFormat.set({
        spaceBefore: 6,
        spaceAfter: 12,
        lineSpacing: 18,
        alignment: "Center"
    });

    await context.sync();
});
```

