The search for ""keepWithNext" "Word.Paragraph" office.js" returned the following summary:
In the Office JavaScript API for Word, **`keepWithNext`** is a property of the **`Word.ParagraphFormat`** class[1]. 

It corresponds to the "Keep with next" pagination option in Microsoft Word[1], which specifies whether a paragraph remains on the same page as the paragraph that follows it when Word repaginates the document[1] (frequently used for headings to prevent them from sitting orphaned at the bottom of a page[2]).

### Usage Example

The following example demonstrates how to access and set `keepWithNext` on a paragraph's format using `Word.run`:

```javascript
Word.run(async (context) => {
    // Get the first paragraph in the document body
    const paragraph = context.document.body.paragraphs.getFirst();

    // Access the paragraphFormat property
    const paragraphFormat = paragraph.paragraphFormat;

    // Set keepWithNext to true
    paragraphFormat.keepWithNext = true;

    // Synchronize the execution with the Word document
    await context.sync();

    console.log("Paragraph has been set to stay with the next paragraph.");
});
```

### Reading the Property

If you need to read whether `keepWithNext` is currently enabled on a paragraph or a style, you must explicitly load the property before calling `context.sync()`[1][3]:

```javascript
Word.run(async (context) => {
    const paragraph = context.document.body.paragraphs.getFirst();
    const paragraphFormat = paragraph.paragraphFormat;

    // Load the specific property you want to read
    paragraphFormat.load("keepWithNext");

    await context.sync();

    console.log(`Keep with next: ${paragraphFormat.keepWithNext}`);
});
```

